            "content": "# Agent instructions — storyproof\n\nLocal visual regression testing for Storybook: capture Chromium screenshots, review baseline/candidate/diff inside Storybook itself, approve baselines as PNGs committed next to the story source. No cloud service.\n\n`CLAUDE.md` and `GEMINI.md` are symlinks to this file.\n\n**Setup, the checks to run, commit conventions, and the AI-assistance policy live in [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md)** — one contract for humans and agents, not two that drift. It is imported here so it loads with this file:\n\n@CONTRIBUTING.md\n\nWhat follows is why the repository is shaped the way it is — the decisions that are expensive to rediscover.\n\n## Layout\n\npnpm workspace monorepo (Node >= 22.12, development pin in `.node-version`; pnpm 10) on Turborepo.\n\n| Path                  | Role                                                              | Own instructions                           |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `packages/storyproof` | The addon — the only published npm package (`storyproof`)         | [AGENTS.md](packages/storyproof/AGENTS.md) |\n| `examples/*`          | Storybook examples: the dev loop, and CI's acceptance fixture     | [AGENTS.md](examples/AGENTS.md)            |\n| `apps/website`        | storyproof.dev site (placeholder, private, framework not chosen)  | —                                          |\n\nThose files are the authority for their areas — don't restate them here.\n\n**The task graph is real, not ceremony.** `examples/*` need `packages/storyproof` to have been **built**, not merely linked, and Storybook cannot hot-reload an addon (its manager bundle compiles once at startup) — `turbo watch` is what rebuilds and restarts it.\n\n## Toolchain decisions\n\nCommand list: [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md#the-loop). These are the parts of it that look wrong until you know wh